<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pereiaslav</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pereyaslav, Pereiaslav-Khmelnytskyi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pereiaslav is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, south-east of Kyiv near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>. As Pereyaslavl it was one of the chief towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> and the seat of a principality guarding the steppe frontier, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> sacked it in 1239. In 1654 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> council held there under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a> accepted the protection of the Russian tsar. It was called Pereiaslav-Khmelnytskyi from 1943 to 2019.</p></div>
